Carried over from Octo Updater, largely unchanged
-------------------------------------------------

Most of what EqUpdater *does* is the original author's work:

  - the torrent-based client sync built on aria2c, including the file
    selection, the protected-file shielding and the locale patching
  - WoW.exe tweak patching and Config.wtf generation
  - the MPQ content-patch engine
  - the addon installer (git-archive zips pinned to a commit)
  - the mod registry and the GitHub/Codeberg release plumbing
  - the hardened TLS context, download-host allowlist and HTTPS-only
    redirect handling
  - atomic config writes and the shared config lock
  - the news and patch-notes feeds
  - the window: its layout, palette, navigation and the look of every page

What EqUpdater changed
----------------------

  - An ownership model. Components are managed, adopted or merely found, and
    only the first two are ever modified automatically.
  - Real version ordering (equpdater/versions.py) in place of comparing two
    version strings for inequality.
  - Commit ancestry (equpdater/gitcompare.py) in place of comparing two shas
    for inequality.
  - Local-modification detection (equpdater/hashing.py).
  - A single update planner (equpdater/planner.py) that every list, badge,
    worker and sweep consults, replacing four independent implementations.
  - Provenance in the configuration schema, and a one-time migration from
    Octo Updater's.
  - Explicit adopt / release / switch-source / force-replace actions, with
    backups.
  - The product identity, and a test suite for the safety rules.

Bundled at runtime, not included here
-------------------------------------

  - aria2c (https://aria2.github.io/) is downloaded at runtime when the client
    needs syncing; it is not redistributed in this repository.
  - certifi is an optional dependency used to supplement the system
    certificate store.

